nking. Revenue (net interest income plus noninterest income) rose 10.7% to $8.2B in 2025. Net interest income rose 12.1% to $6.0B and noninterest income rose 7.0% to $2.2B; noninterest expense rose 6.4%, and the provision for credit losses was $463M, versus $420M.","Net income to common rose 15.9% to $2.1B, or $1.39 per diluted share, and the efficiency ratio was 59.3% versus 61.7%. Huntington returned $908M through dividends."],"highlights":["Revenue rose 10.7% to $8.2B.","Net interest income rose 12.1%.","Noninterest income rose 7.0% to $2.2B.","Net income to common rose 15.9% to $2.1B."],"watch":["Credit-loss provision rose 10.2% to $463M.","Unusual items cost $167M before tax.","Net interest income depends on interest rates.","Noninterest expense was $4.8B, up 6.4%."],"table":[["Total revenue",8.155,7.367,1],["Net interest income",5.991,5.345],["Noninterest income",2.164,2.022],["Noninterest expense",4.837,4.544],["Provision for credit losses",0.463,0.42],["Other items, net",-0.167,0.0],["Pre-tax income",2.688,2.403,1],["Income tax",0.459,0.443],["Noncontrolling interests",-0.018,-0.02],["Preferred dividends & other",-0.124,0.139],["Net income to common",2.087,1.801,1],["Diluted EPS ($)",1.39,1.22,0,"eps"],["Book value per share ($)",13.784877,12.211449,0,"eps"]],"sources":[["Huntington Bancshares Incorporated Form 10-K filings (SEC EDGAR)","https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0000049196&type=10-K"],["Huntington financial statements (StockAnalysis)","https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/hban/financials/"]]},"video":{"revenueLine":{"cap":"Net interest income was 73% of revenue.","say":"Net interest income made up 73 percent of revenue."},"spotlights":[{"kicker":"Revenue","big":"$8.2B","sub":"revenue · +10.7%","lines":["Net interest income $6.0B","Noninterest income $2.2B"],"cap":"Revenue rose 10.7% to $8.2B.","say":"Revenue rose 10.7% to $8.2B."},{"kicker":"Per share","big":"$1.39","sub":"diluted EPS · +13.9%","lines":["Net income to common